---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How DragBuilder collects, uses, stores and shares personal data, including data received from Google APIs."
  updated="October 8, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains what personal data DragBuilder ("DragBuilder", "we", "us") collects when you use
    the DragBuilder website at <a href="https://dragbuilder.io">dragbuilder.io</a>, the web app at
    <a href="https://app.dragbuilder.io">app.dragbuilder.io</a>, and the DragBuilder desktop applications
    (together, the "Service"), how we use it, and the choices you have.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
  <p>
    DragBuilder is the controller of the personal data described here. You can reach us at
    <a href="mailto:admin@dragbuilder.io">admin@dragbuilder.io</a> for any question about this policy or your data.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
  <h3>Account data</h3>
  <p>
    When you sign in with Google, Apple, GitHub or Microsoft, we receive the basic profile your provider shares:
    your name, email address, profile picture and a provider-specific user identifier. We use it to create and
    recognize your account. We never receive or store your password for those providers.
  </p>
  <h3>Content you create</h3>
  <p>
    Your DragBuilder projects (screens, components, settings and generated app code) and the files you upload to
    them, such as launcher icons, splash images and other assets. We store this content so that you can open it from
    any device and so that we can build and publish your apps when you ask us to.
  </p>
  <h3>Publishing and signing credentials</h3>
  <p>
    If you use the publishing features, you may provide a Google Play service account key, an App Store Connect API
    key and identifiers, and we generate and store an Android signing key (keystore) and its passwords for each of your
    projects. These credentials are used only to build, sign and publish your own apps at your request.
  </p>
  <h3>Billing data</h3>
  <p>
    Payments are handled by our payment provider, Paddle, which acts as the merchant of record. We receive your
    subscription status, plan, billing email and related identifiers. We do not receive or store your full payment
    card number.
  </p>
  <h3>Support and device information</h3>
  <p>
    If you contact support we keep the tickets and messages you send. We also record the devices you sign in from (a
    device identifier, name and the last time it was used) so that we can alert you when a new device signs in to your
    account.
  </p>
  <h3>Usage and diagnostics</h3>
  <p>
    We collect product analytics (which features are used) and error reports so that we can fix bugs and improve the
    Service. This data may include your user identifier, your device and browser type, and technical details about an
    error.
  </p>
  <h3>AI features</h3>
  <p>
    When you use the built-in AI assistant, the instructions you type and the relevant part of your project are sent to
    our AI provider so that it can generate a response. We do not use this content to advertise to you.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Data we receive from Google</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Signing in.</strong> When you choose "Sign in with Google" we request only the basic information
    needed to identify you: your name, email address and profile picture.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Connecting your Firebase / Google Cloud project (desktop app).</strong> If you choose to connect a
    Firebase or Google Cloud project, the desktop app asks for additional permissions to act in your own project on
    your behalf: <em>Firebase</em> (<code>auth/firebase</code>), <em>Google Cloud Platform</em>
    (<code>auth/cloud-platform</code>) and <em>Google Cloud Storage read/write</em>
    (<code>auth/devstorage.read_write</code>). We use them only to create and configure the Firebase apps and
    resources that you ask DragBuilder to set up in your project. The access token is used to perform those actions;
    we do not use it for any other purpose, and you can revoke access at any time at
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    DragBuilder's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements. We do not sell Google user data, do not use it for advertising, and do not
    allow people to read it except as needed to provide the features you request, for security, or to comply with law.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How we use your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide, operate and secure the Service, and to build and publish your apps when you ask.</li>
    <li>To process payments and manage your subscription.</li>
    <li>To send service emails: sign-in alerts for new devices, publishing results, billing and support replies.</li>
    <li>To provide support and respond to your requests.</li>
    <li>To understand how the Service is used, fix errors and improve it.</li>
    <li>To detect and prevent fraud, abuse and security incidents, and to comply with legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Who we share data with</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal data. We share it only with service providers that process it on our behalf, strictly
    to run the Service:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Google Cloud / Firebase</td><td>Hosting, file storage and backend functions</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Authentication, database (accounts, subscriptions, tickets, devices)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Codemagic and GitHub</td><td>Building your mobile apps when you ask us to publish them</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Paddle</td><td>Payments, taxes and invoicing</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Resend</td><td>Sending service emails</td></tr>
      <tr><td>PostHog and Sentry</td><td>Product analytics and error reporting</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Delivery and security of the website and web app</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Anthropic</td><td>Powering the AI assistant</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information if required by law, or to protect the rights, safety and security of our users
    and the Service. If DragBuilder is involved in a merger or sale, data may be transferred as part of it, and we
    will tell you beforehand.
  </p>

  <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Our providers operate in several countries, including the United States. When your data is transferred outside
    your country we rely on appropriate safeguards, such as the contractual protections offered by those providers.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your account and project data while your account is active. When you delete your account, we delete
    your projects and personal data, except what we must keep for legal, tax or security reasons (for example billing
    records). Backups are removed on a rolling basis.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Your projects and credentials are stored in private cloud storage and are reachable only through your
    authenticated account. Traffic to the Service is encrypted in transit. No system is perfectly secure, so we also
    recommend that you protect your sign-in provider account, and that you keep a copy of your Android signing key,
    since it is needed to update your app.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights and choices</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, export or delete your personal data, to
    object to or restrict some processing, and to withdraw consent. You can delete your account from within the app,
    and you can export your projects at any time. To exercise any right, or to ask us for a copy of your data, write
    to <a href="mailto:admin@dragbuilder.io">admin@dragbuilder.io</a>. You may also lodge a complaint with your local
    data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The Service is not directed to children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect their personal data. If you
    believe a child has given us data, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    The website and web app use cookies and local storage that are needed to keep you signed in and remember your
    preferences, and analytics tools described above. You can control cookies in your browser settings; blocking the
    essential ones may prevent you from signing in.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the Service changes. We will post the new version here with a new "Last updated"
    date, and we will notify you of material changes by email or within the app.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:admin@dragbuilder.io">admin@dragbuilder.io</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
